{
 "$comment": "Crucial Ballistix (OpenRGB d4798c12 CrucialController.cpp / CrucialControllerDetect.cpp / RGBController_Crucial.cpp), worked out from the C++ (each register access written out from CrucialController.cpp, the per-LED lists expanded mechanically), not by running the plugin. Wire transfers are [op, command, value]: 'ww' SMBus Write Word (value as the 16-bit word; LSB goes first on the wire), 'wb' Write Byte Data, 'blk' SMBus Block Write (the data; the count byte is its length), 'rb' Read Byte Data, 'rx' Receive Byte (no command). A register access is Write Word to command 0x00 with the register byte-swapped ((reg << 8) & 0xFF00 | reg >> 8), then Write Byte 0x01 (write), Read Byte 0x81 (read) or Block Write 0x03. Register-level lists are [register, value] pairs, each one such access.",
